        "id": 52178,
        "name": "waedens",
        "username": "waedens",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/b3f665/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-16T18:01:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ok another question.&nbsp;</p><p>SubZero has a power that allows him to deal 1 cold damage to 3 non-hero targets. At the end of his turn he must deal x fire damage to himself, where x = the total amount of cold damage he delt this turn. (I think I got that correct)</p><p>He also has an ongoing card that says anytime he takes fire damage he deals that much cold damage to 1 target.&nbsp;</p><p>Doesn't that set up a loop? Or do we just say the one card's effect is over so when the second effect comes into play it doesn't trigger more fire damage to SubZero?</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:26:00.178Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
